li, and A. Cerutti. <year>2003</year>. EBV-encoded latent membrane protein 1 cooperates with BAFF/BLyS and APRIL to induce T cell-independent Ig heavy chain class switching. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>171</volume>:<fpage>5215</fpage>&#x02013;5224.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14607922</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Gourzi, P., T. Leonova, and F.N. Papavasiliou. <year>2006</year>. A role for activation-induced cytidine deaminase in the host response against a transforming retrovirus. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>24</volume>:<fpage>779</fpage>&#x02013;786.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16782033</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kawai, T., and S. Akira. <year>2006</year>. Innate immune recognition of viral infection. <source>Nat. Immunol.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>131</fpage>&#x02013;137.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16424890</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Takeda, K., and S. Akira. <year>2004</year>. TLR signaling pathways. <source>Semin. Immunol.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>3</fpage>&#x02013;9.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14751757</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Pasare, C., and R. Medzhitov. <year>2005</year>. Control of B-cell responses by Toll-like receptors. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>438</volume>:<fpage>364</fpage>&#x02013;368.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16292312</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Gavin, A.L., K. Hoebe, B. Duong, T. Ota, C. Martin, B. Beutler, and D. Nemazee. <year>2006</year>. Adjuvant-enhanced antibody responses in the absence of toll-like receptor signaling. <source>Science.</source> <volume>314</volume>:<fpage>1936</fpage>&#x02013;1938.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17185603</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><label>25</labe